Story Title: Enable Valkey or Redis Caching for Graphbase Local Federation Runtime

Story Description: As a Platform Engineer, I want to enable Valkey or Redis configuration in local Graphbase runtime, so that we can validate Valkey backend caching behavior for local query federation POC. 

The story proves cache feasibility behavior and configuration pattern at POC level.

In Scope: 

Valkey or Redis container runs via docker-compose with persistence.

 Run configured to use Valkey endpoint through environment config. 

Graphbase cache configuration. 

Cache behavior validation (entity or query). 

TTL or Cache tagging at POC level. 

Documentation updated with cache setup and verification flow. 

Cache persistence across gateway restart verified at retained keyspaces.

Acceptance Criteria: 

Redis or Valkey runs alongside Graphbase via docker-compose. 

Runtime uses Valkey backend caching. 

Repeat queries return cached response. 

Cache TTL or tagging behavior is demonstrated. 

Cache survives runtime restart when applicable. 

Readme updated with cache configuration details.

note

 If backend mock APIs are down, cache validation queries fail because source data cannot be fetched on initial miss. POC accepted for local feasibility of Valkey caching in federation runtime.